## Critical dependencies

- **Mode cache** (`NavMeshModeCache`) — `_active_osm_mode()` resolves `walking` / `wheelchair` so `wheelchair` mode hides `steps` segments automatically. Same instance the production CU accessibility toggle uses.
- **`OsmGraphService`** — owned by `younite.osm_navigation_extension`. We never duplicate the graph; we cache a per-mode filtered subgraph (`_visible_adj`, `_visible_node_pos`) at overlay-on time and rebuild it on mode change.
- **`NavMeshRouteService`** — only used to call `stop_route(player)` so its in-flight calculation doesn't overwrite our waypoints.
- **`PointClickAutoMover`** (in `younite.usd_viewer_player_core_extension`) — consumes `navmeshRouteWaypoints` for `routeId === "player"`. Speed comes from `segmentSpeeds × base_speed`.

