## Tuning knobs (all in `osm_route_overlay/constants.py`)

| Constant | Default | Knob |
|---|---|---|
| `OVERLAY_COLOR` | `(0.32, 0.62, 0.95)` | Tinted-glass blue. Stay cool / desaturated; saturated cyans read as paint stripe |
| `OVERLAY_OPACITY` | 0.22 | True translucency. Below 0.18 disappears over bright pavement; above 0.30 starts reading opaque |
| `OVERLAY_EMISSIVE_GAIN` | 0.06 | Self-lit boost. Keep < 0.10 of diffuse — emissive is not modulated by opacity |
| `OVERLAY_ROUGHNESS` | 0.18 | Specular sharpness. >0.50 reads as chalk/matte; <0.10 produces denoiser flicker on a 1.1 m wide surface |
| `OVERLAY_WIDTH_CM` | 110.0 | Surface width — touch-target vs visual flooding |
| `OVERLAY_HOVER_CM` | 35.0 | Hover above ground. Must stay below CCT `stepOffset` (40 cm) |
| `SNAP_PROXIMITY_CM` | 90.0 | Off-route, off-NavMesh / "world" click → route snap radius (slightly > half-width). Used **only** when the NavMesh is too far to handle the click |
| `NAVMESH_TOLERANCE_CM` (in `route_composer.types`) | 50.0 | Terrain-click NavMesh-priority threshold. Click within this XZ distance of the NavMesh → re-emit `navigation.requestPoint`. **Re-used** here, not duplicated |
| `OSM_ROUTE_WALK_SPEED` | 12.0 | Auto-mover base-speed multiplier; matches bird-eye composer pace |
| `AT_JUNCTION_RADIUS_CM` | 200.0 | Player-near-junction shortcut radius for auto-advance |
| `NEAR_ROUTE_RADIUS_CM` | 250.0 | Max distance to attach auto-advance to a route |
| `MAX_AUTO_ADVANCE_HOPS` | 64 | Chain-walker runaway guard. Re-used by `player_chain_edges` for same-chain detection |

